{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/547089-conversion-guide","id":547089,"title":"Conversion Guide","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-09T08:26:25-07:00","id":547089,"title":"Conversion Guide","content":"Will there be one for when Sardonyx drops? And would there also be one for the Aeoniverse?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T09:01:37-07:00","id":547120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/547089-conversion-guide#post547089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will there be one for when Sardonyx drops?</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> We're making strong - almost radical - changes to how Scion works. Knacks, Purviews, Scaling, Fate, Fatebinding, Archetypes, Legend, pantheons, <i>types </i>of Scion - all different. A conversion guide would basically boil down to a large series of judgment calls and be dependent on you guys eyeballing your own stuff anyways.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And would there also be one for the Aeoniverse? </div> </div> </div>Not my call, but I'll ask Ian.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T09:17:23-07:00","id":547133,"title":"","content":"Well, thanks a lot for the concise answer. I ask because I do have a Scion group and they were asking if they could still play their old characters. Fortunately, the players are mature enough. If I tell them that we are just rebooting them, then they have already accepted that as a possibility. <br /> And if Ian does answer you, then thanks for passing on anything to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T16:32:40-07:00","id":547679,"title":"","content":"I'm not planning on one. As Neall says it would largely be up to individual taste, and putting a document together would take time away from writing/developing the books. They've been delayed long enough. If fans want to put something together, they're welcome to it.<br /> <br /> If you want, you could still allow them to play the &quot;same&quot; characters. Just hand them the new character creation rules and, say, 50 XP or whatever sounds reasonable. They might not be exactly the same as the old ones, but close enough. If it were an Aberrant game, it might give me an excuse to run an epic Secret Wars/Crisis on Infinite Earths/Blackest Night -style storyline, with the &quot;before&quot; universe in the old rules, and the &quot;after&quot; universe in the new rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T16:47:08-07:00","id":547714,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the reply, Ian. I am going to do a reboot. It allows me to right the wrongs of the first Chronicle. My players knew it was a possibility. The sweet part was when I told them that we can play Scions pre-Visitation. We love doing that. <br /> As far as Aeoniverse goes, I have not had a chance to run them through any games of it. So they are not missing out on anything there. I was mainly asking for when I go to run a game and wanted to use some old NPC's. I will just go ahead and redo them from the ground up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T16:56:20-07:00","id":547735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/547089-conversion-guide?p=547120#post547120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No.<br /> <br /> We're making strong - almost radical - changes to how Scion works. Knacks, Purviews, Scaling, Fate, Fatebinding, Archetypes, Legend, pantheons, <i>types </i>of Scion - all different. A conversion guide would basically boil down to a large series of judgment calls and be dependent on you guys eyeballing your own stuff anyways.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Not my call, but I'll ask Ian.</div> </div> </div> </div>Types of Scion?<br /> <br /> Is this like how there's been mention of Hero children of two Gods alongside more &quot;traditional&quot; one mortal one divine parent Scions, or is this something new entirely?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/ksr/avatars/3507685/Exalted_Back.small.jpg?1370109312\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <hr />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/446-nervaqus987","name":"Nervaqus987","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar446_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T18:34:46-07:00","id":547849,"title":"","content":"Evidently we'll be given the chance of playing Einerjar, Amazons, Elves, Satyrs and maybe even Minotaurs (and hopefully THEIR descendants)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T20:48:04-07:00","id":547946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nervaqus987</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/547089-conversion-guide?p=547735#post547735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Types of Scion?<br /> <br /> Is this like how there's been mention of Hero children of two Gods alongside more &quot;traditional&quot; one mortal one divine parent Scions, or is this something new entirely?</div> </div> </div> </div>Protip: look at the end of the new Sardonyx blog.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}